    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one actual test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are the base class and a helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, responding with **400 Bad Request**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`FutureRegistrationDateException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending date, mirroring the existing `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` pattern.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectFutureRegistrationDate(...)` guard called in `addOwner` *before* the null-default and business-day roll, so it validates the date exactly as supplied. A `null` date (defaulted to today) and any date on or before today are accepted; a future date throws.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `FutureRegistrationDateException` that returns 400 with the standard `ProblemDetail` body and `errors: [\"registrationDate\"]`, consistent with the other owner-field handlers.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (including the new `errorRejectsFutureDate`) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
